{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_23e5e36be1bea4a5d315788e05af8ba3eb6e80a3dea2483e106ebe7081911aca","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a9071bed6d395d50a2ae69cad25ebc2afae3b1b3986a47dcb69aba96a827313","slc_cc12aeaf502f4c7cc1017c7aee05979e58c94f1f4cd1e5bf195d7253597d361f","slc_d8623e8f8e2b8554f1838717cfca2ebc602cc5628e60ae008208a6024927c264"],"source_ids":["src_eb9be3928d8e58ea85b5a009d3e6f303"],"text":"Fusil is configured entirely through command-line options, grouped into categories like Input, Running, Fuzzing, OOM Fuzzing, and Logging; a former fusil.conf file mechanism was removed, making CLI options the single source of truth.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2f65d5ac2fd1e36d6113b6e549adcd9301c26808a6727e646ad7b866084866a3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0cb67872ff79f26f5ff3098101ccb9610842400362784cd1efa4f4e37a62a5e6","slc_11b2aed5f1c9cbbb7cc09c79849a44ce6d5a37c34fd095fb4c24d180f43ff62e","slc_19e69361162e0f7bfa301e66563ca281180636b02a7a2a19eb7d5db3eac2e460","slc_71ca2a6661eac7be5bef150d8fcdeee30b21c7e39fc5a431bcc6365f0d1aa35a","slc_80cae617fa2fefc9bc2e0c68e44dc04eef6548f87224a082d127fb8eb57c05b4"],"source_ids":["src_3b4da4666499505685025435c2d2b7cd"],"text":"The fusil.c_tools module provides C code generation utilities: CodeC with addMain()/addFunction() for building functions, a compile() method, and FuzzyFunctionC with value generators like createInt32, createString, and createRandomBytes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_36885c75776835396edd255e54c040c5cbc5b884977ec8d14c17afb9f3ac853f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5b81c827c5a55fe695592acef8c11930de638ab1f1882e7c0a9ce3d0b411dbb0"],"source_ids":["src_d36a932791495f3ca67aa940900a09c0"],"text":"By default the fuzzer expects a dedicated unprivileged fusil user/group to drop privileges to; the --unsafe flag instead runs fuzzed children as the current user.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4592bb549b23f83420a8400a6ca4ce32f0fd9ec8acde3da26ae2be218a1d6006","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9be97c4c7373e296f10ee108634c913c2fe551e487c18a8bc069438294582cb8"],"source_ids":["src_eb9be3928d8e58ea85b5a009d3e6f303"],"text":"A few settings lack CLI flags — session scoring thresholds, the memory limit, and the dedicated fusil-user sandbox user/group — and live as constants in fusil/config.py's FusilConfig class.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_587c3096b2ca3b931c2af98fc7ee5650290eadd2b82b1fd0f197eb8ea7092126","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8c02b8ab5b9c609cb90b219528e270e018ba9463ec2ee842d90de47fdc259bf1","slc_b4bf0ba0e6d527da568975fc40b5de9e9e78d4d7d301ac7f9ad24698abf288ea"],"source_ids":["src_9c2b474ba6a454a294b9cb10c829ae5d"],"text":"The memory cap was made ASan-safe: RLIMIT_AS is skipped when an ASan target is auto-detected or --no-memory-limit is set (since ASan reserves ~20 TB of virtual address space), relying on an external cgroup cap, while core-dump/nproc/nice limits are kept in all cases.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_60b3ac5775ed024c98b40a56ae98239d58535e737f39c04012ecf9226edc2c6f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9ff518fbe047a4d10b06d5bb50a08fde3287e3505aa346adada0be7592fe1888"],"source_ids":["src_d36a932791495f3ca67aa940900a09c0"],"text":"Fusil is a revival of Victor Stinner's fuzzing framework; only the Python fuzzing path is actively developed and tested, targeting crashes in CPython, C extensions, the Tier-2 JIT, and OOM error paths.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_65ebc804fcc6cb3425d37d2aeb92ba373e5919dcbd8e1f139c5379484c53d1d7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4ca607f9119bef357e100d5607c1dd668706d14f230db6df9bab31f41398ae84","slc_52ca1b7f9c5744835d5edb0d07ce6a3b5ef2511a0646865f48d4c8f0749e6d03"],"source_ids":["src_d36a932791495f3ca67aa940900a09c0"],"text":"Fusil requires Python 3.13+ and python-ptrace; numpy and h5py are optional extras supporting the argument generator, installed via pip install -e '.[numpy,h5py]'.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7889ad8225b9dc8a01328b15aa024f432e59bf3feb0a542921defac6ac53f608","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_05e4cedacb743b9077eaa1ba616b051b617e5952056fb65bb07410b342bf83a1"],"source_ids":["src_d36a932791495f3ca67aa940900a09c0"],"text":"Each session generates a standalone test script, runs it as a sandboxed child process with memory/cpu/process limits, dropped privileges, and redirected output, watching for crash signals and patterns like 'Fatal Python error' or AddressSanitizer output.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_80d223c57a2389a5c1e8eb4ee4960b0d1df8c97045dcf8c69fb4f890922b05ee","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1ae0a0e4dcd512f984f5733e2517d74e4d8a93d452aaf9b9fd133d5a164b012b","slc_3e59ed9997a52dcaae5dae718d18b1aebbeee76bda282b56f4e607b6f47391d8","slc_b5efbb05c9ac284858a61a83b8cc0a636d166bf24979b6951c4b71a7bca2e700","slc_b73eee27af1d46b166085d2c0f48126f0770079d8124c579d1f6401ad8440e4b"],"source_ids":["src_48bdd13eb10a5ab6bb8176ba253bd69f"],"text":"Agents are objects that send and receive messages, are inactive by default until activate() is called, expose a live() method invoked each session step, and register event handlers via on_EVENT-style method names.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_aa563e86ab6aca14362c8cb5e3bc1076e43a953299049eae66c3154e5d4ac9b1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"devdanzin/fusil@a7aa4e94bd84 snapshot fe73214caf262697","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e74bac349ce21eebd278d69647d37ebcb295bc2ed978fa6ddb6cb0c1be36e532"],"source_ids":["src_d36a932791495f3ca67aa940900a09c0"],"text":"Historical non-Python fuzzers (firefox, php, mplayer) and subsystems like network, file/process mangling, and X11 are legacy and out of scope, kept under notworking/ directories and may not work as-is.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
